IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `rra-nouns`
IMPORT `rra-logic`
IMPORT `rra-part1-preliminary`

-- Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal
-- consolidation in force from 1 July 2022 -- PART 5 GENERAL (ss 9 to 13).
--
-- Answers are MAYBE BOOLEAN: JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE where the text itself says yes / no (the words quoted at that branch),
-- NOTHING where it does not (tagged `NOTHING-kind (...)`).  Section 12 (the regulation-making power) and section 10(3)
-- (the power to prescribe compoundable offences) are powers to make law, not rules a case can be asked of: see the
-- coverage table in NOTES.md.  What the regulations prescribe is not among the sources.

§ `Part 5 -- General`

§§ `Section 9 -- Powers of the Commissioner and investigating officers`

-- "power to do all or any of the following": each of the seven is a separate grant, and the Commissioner or an
-- investigating officer may do any one, some or all of them (fork F14).  The list is the Act's; any other power is not
-- granted by this subsection.
-- src:967 | 9.—(1) The Commissioner or any investigating officer has, for the
-- src:969 | purposes of this Act, power to do all or any of the following:
-- src:971 | (a) enter without previous notice at any reasonable time any
-- src:972 | place of employment for the purposes of conducting any
-- src:973 | audit which is deemed necessary by the Minister, or make
-- src:974 | such inquiry into the terms and conditions of employment
-- src:975 | of any employee as the Commissioner or investigating
-- src:976 | officer thinks fit;
@ref s 9(1) (src:967-976)
GIVEN `the person is the Commissioner or an investigating officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the power is exercised for the purposes of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      power IS A `Power under section 9(1)`
      `it is at a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(1) the person has the power` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the person is the Commissioner or an investigating officer` AND `the power is exercised for the purposes of this Act`)
    THEN
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is of "The Commissioner or any investigating officer" "for the purposes of this Act"
        NOTHING
    ELSE
        CONSIDER power
        WHEN `enter a place of employment without previous notice to conduct an audit or make an inquiry` THEN
            IF `it is at a reasonable time`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE
                -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power to enter is "at any reasonable time"; the time is not reasonable
                NOTHING
        WHEN `examine a person orally` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `require the employer to produce an employee together with a contract of service or other document` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `make copies of a document required to be produced` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `take or remove a document for the purposes of investigations` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `take photographs or audio or video recordings of the premises and of persons` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `require a person to produce an article and take it into custody` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the subsection gives "power to do all or any of the following"; it does not say that the person has no other power
        WHEN `another power` THEN NOTHING

-- src:978 | (b) examine orally any person supposed to be acquainted with
-- src:979 | the facts and circumstances relevant to the carrying out of
-- src:980 | the provisions of this Act, and reduce into writing the
-- src:981 | answer given or statement made by the person who is
-- src:988 | bound to state truly the facts and circumstances with which
-- src:989 | the person is acquainted, and the statement made by the
-- src:990 | person must be read over to him or her and must, after
-- src:991 | correction, be signed by the person;
@ref s 9(1)(b) (src:978-991)
GIVEN `the person is supposed to be acquainted with the facts and circumstances relevant to the carrying out of the provisions of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is examined orally by the Commissioner or an investigating officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(1)(b) the person examined is bound to state truly the facts and circumstances` MEANS
    IF `the person is supposed to be acquainted with the facts and circumstances relevant to the carrying out of the provisions of this Act` AND `the person is examined orally by the Commissioner or an investigating officer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is of a person "supposed to be acquainted with the facts and circumstances relevant to the carrying out of the provisions of this Act" who is examined orally
        NOTHING

-- src:993 | (c) require the employer to produce before the Commissioner
-- src:994 | or investigating officer any other employee employed by
-- src:995 | the employer together with any contract of service or other
-- src:996 | document concerning the employment;
@ref s 9(1)(c) (src:993-996)
GIVEN `the person is the Commissioner or an investigating officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person asked is the employer of the other employee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(1)(c) the Commissioner or investigating officer may require the employer to produce the employee and the documents` MEANS
    IF `the person is the Commissioner or an investigating officer` AND `the person asked is the employer of the other employee`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is to "require the employer to produce before the Commissioner or investigating officer any other employee employed by the employer together with any contract of service or other document concerning the employment"
        NOTHING

-- src:1010 | (g) require any person to produce any article which is relevant
-- src:1011 | to any investigation carried out under this Act and, if
-- src:1012 | necessary, to take into custody any such article.
@ref s 9(1)(g) (src:1010-1012)
GIVEN `the person is the Commissioner or an investigating officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the article is relevant to an investigation carried out under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(1)(g) the Commissioner or investigating officer may require a person to produce the article` MEANS
    IF `the person is the Commissioner or an investigating officer` AND `the article is relevant to an investigation carried out under this Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is to "require any person to produce any article which is relevant to any investigation carried out under this Act"
        NOTHING

-- src:1014 | (2) Any person who hinders or obstructs an investigating officer in
-- src:1015 | the exercise of the power under this section or makes to an
-- src:1016 | investigating officer exercising the power under this section a
-- src:1017 | statement either orally or in writing which is false in any material
-- src:1018 | particular shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on
-- src:1019 | conviction to a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a
-- src:1020 | term not exceeding 6 months or to both.
@ref s 9(2) (src:1014-1020)
GIVEN `the person hinders or obstructs an investigating officer in the exercise of the power under section 9` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person makes to an investigating officer exercising the power a statement, orally or in writing, which is false in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(2) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the person hinders or obstructs an investigating officer in the exercise of the power under section 9` OR `the person makes to an investigating officer exercising the power a statement, orally or in writing, which is false in a material particular`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the offence is of a person who "hinders or obstructs an investigating officer in the exercise of the power under this section or makes ... a statement ... which is false in any material particular"
        NOTHING

@ref s 9(2) (src:1014-1020)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 9(2) the penalty on conviction` MEANS Penalty OF 5_000, 6

@ref s 9(2) (src:1014-1020)
GIVEN `the person has been convicted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fine in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the imprisonment in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(2) the sentence is within the penalty` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person has been convicted`
    THEN
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the penalty is one the person is "liable on conviction" to; there has been no conviction
        NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the fine and the term are within the ceilings` (`s 9(2) the penalty on conviction`) `the fine in dollars` `the imprisonment in months`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or to both"
            JUST FALSE

§§ `Section 9A -- Investigations of complaints and offences`

-- src:1024 | 9A.—(1) Whenever —
-- src:1026 | (a) the Minister, the Commissioner or an investigating officer
-- src:1027 | has reasonable grounds for believing that an offence under
-- src:1028 | this Act has been committed;
-- src:1030 | (b) the Minister, the Commissioner or an investigating officer
-- src:1031 | wishes to inquire into any matter for which provision is
-- src:1033 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 1/7/2022
-- src:1034 | Retirement and Re-employment
-- src:1036 | 21 Act 1993 2020 Ed.
-- src:1038 | made by this Act or any dispute as to such matter, or any
-- src:1039 | matter connected with an investigation; or
-- src:1041 | (c) any person complains of any breach of any provision of
-- src:1042 | this Act,
-- src:1044 | the Minister, the Commissioner or the investigating officer (as the
-- src:1045 | case may be) may summon any person whom he or she has reason to
-- src:1046 | believe can give information regarding the subject matter of the
-- src:1047 | inquiry or complaint, and the person so summoned is legally bound to
-- src:1048 | attend at the time and place specified in the summons to furnish
@ref s 9A(1) (src:1024-1048)
GIVEN `the person acting is the Minister, the Commissioner or an investigating officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are reasonable grounds for believing that an offence under this Act has been committed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acting wishes to inquire into a matter for which provision is made by this Act, or a dispute as to such a matter, or a matter connected with an investigation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a person complains of a breach of a provision of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acting has reason to believe that the person can give information regarding the subject matter of the inquiry or complaint` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9A(1) the person acting may summon the person` MEANS
    IF `the person acting is the Minister, the Commissioner or an investigating officer` AND (`there are reasonable grounds for believing that an offence under this Act has been committed` OR `the person acting wishes to inquire into a matter for which provision is made by this Act, or a dispute as to such a matter, or a matter connected with an investigation` OR `a person complains of a breach of a provision of this Act`) AND `the person acting has reason to believe that the person can give information regarding the subject matter of the inquiry or complaint`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is of the Minister, the Commissioner or an investigating officer, "Whenever" one of the three grounds exists, to "summon any person whom he or she has reason to believe can give information regarding the subject matter of the inquiry or complaint"
        NOTHING

-- src:1044 | the Minister, the Commissioner or the investigating officer (as the
-- src:1045 | case may be) may summon any person whom he or she has reason to
-- src:1046 | believe can give information regarding the subject matter of the
-- src:1047 | inquiry or complaint, and the person so summoned is legally bound to
-- src:1048 | attend at the time and place specified in the summons to furnish
-- src:1049 | information or documents, produce any article or give statements, and
-- src:1050 | to answer truthfully all questions which the Minister, the
-- src:1051 | Commissioner or the investigating officer (as the case may be)
-- src:1052 | may put to the person.
@ref s 9A(1) summons (src:1044-1052)
GIVEN `the person was summoned under section 9A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9A(1) the person summoned is legally bound to attend and to answer truthfully` MEANS
    IF `the person was summoned under section 9A(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is of "the person so summoned"
        NOTHING

-- The summons specifies the time and place; the days until then, counted from the day the person is summoned (day 0), are an input.
@ref s 9A(1) summons (src:1044-1052)
GIVEN `the number of days until the time specified in the summons` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`s 9A(1) the person summoned must attend at the time and place specified in the summons` MEANS
    PARTY `A person summoned`
    MUST `attend as the summons requires`
    WITHIN `the number of days until the time specified in the summons`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `A person summoned` BECAUSE "s 9A(1): the person summoned did not attend at the time and place specified in the summons"

-- src:1054 | (2) Any person who in any way wilfully obstructs the service of or
-- src:1055 | obedience to such summons, and any person summoned who neglects
-- src:1056 | to attend as required in such summons, shall be guilty of an offence.
@ref s 9A(2) (src:1054-1056)
GIVEN `the person in any way wilfully obstructs the service of or obedience to the summons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person summoned neglects to attend as required in the summons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9A(2) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the person in any way wilfully obstructs the service of or obedience to the summons` OR `the person summoned neglects to attend as required in the summons`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the offence is of "any person who in any way wilfully obstructs the service of or obedience to such summons" and of "any person summoned who neglects to attend as required in such summons"
        NOTHING

-- src:1058 | (3) The Commissioner or investigating officer has the power to
-- src:1059 | report any failure by such person to attend as required by the
-- src:1060 | summons under subsection (2) to a Magistrate, who may thereupon
-- src:1061 | issue a warrant to secure the attendance of that person as required by
-- src:1062 | the summons.
@ref s 9A(3) (src:1058-1062)
GIVEN `the person summoned failed to attend as required by the summons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9A(3) the Commissioner or investigating officer may report the failure to a Magistrate, who may issue a warrant to secure the attendance` MEANS
    IF `the person summoned failed to attend as required by the summons`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is "to report any failure by such person to attend as required by the summons"
        NOTHING

§§ `Section 9B -- Obstructing employee, etc.`

-- src:1066 | 9B.—(1) An employer or other person who in any way obstructs
-- src:1067 | any employee in appearing before the Commissioner pursuant to any
-- src:1068 | summons issued under this Act shall be guilty of an offence and shall
-- src:1069 | be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to
-- src:1070 | imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or to both.
@ref s 9B(1) (src:1066-1070)
GIVEN `the person is an employer or other person who in any way obstructs an employee in appearing before the Commissioner pursuant to a summons issued under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9B(1) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the person is an employer or other person who in any way obstructs an employee in appearing before the Commissioner pursuant to a summons issued under this Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the offence is of "An employer or other person who in any way obstructs any employee in appearing before the Commissioner pursuant to any summons issued under this Act"
        NOTHING

@ref s 9B(1) (src:1066-1070)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 9B(1) the penalty on conviction` MEANS Penalty OF 5_000, 6

@ref s 9B(1) (src:1066-1070)
GIVEN `the person has been convicted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fine in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the imprisonment in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9B(1) the sentence is within the penalty` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person has been convicted`
    THEN
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the penalty is one the person is "liable on conviction" to; there has been no conviction
        NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the fine and the term are within the ceilings` (`s 9B(1) the penalty on conviction`) `the fine in dollars` `the imprisonment in months`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or to both"
            JUST FALSE

-- src:1072 | (2) A person who wilfully obstructs or impedes any entry, inquiry
-- src:1073 | or investigation made under this Act for which no penalty is expressly
-- src:1074 | provided shall be guilty of an offence.
@ref s 9B(2) (src:1072-1074)
GIVEN `the person wilfully obstructs or impedes an entry, inquiry or investigation made under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a penalty is expressly provided for it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9B(2) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the person wilfully obstructs or impedes an entry, inquiry or investigation made under this Act` AND (NOT `a penalty is expressly provided for it`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the offence is of a person who "wilfully obstructs or impedes any entry, inquiry or investigation made under this Act for which no penalty is expressly provided"
        NOTHING

§§ `Section 9C -- Penalties`

-- "for a subsequent offence under the same section": the dearer ceilings.
-- src:1078 | 9C. A person who is guilty of any breach or any offence under this
-- src:1079 | Act for which no penalty is otherwise provided shall be liable on
-- src:1080 | conviction to a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a
-- src:1082 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 1/7/2022
-- src:1083 | Retirement and Re-employment
-- src:1085 | 2020 Ed. Act 1993 22
-- src:1087 | term not exceeding 6 months or to both, and for a subsequent offence
-- src:1088 | under the same section to a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to
-- src:1089 | imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or to both.
@ref s 9C (src:1078-1089)
GIVEN `the offence is a subsequent offence under the same section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 9C the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    IF `the offence is a subsequent offence under the same section`
    THEN Penalty OF 10_000, 12
    ELSE Penalty OF 5_000, 6

@ref s 9C (src:1078-1089)
GIVEN `the person is guilty of a breach or an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a penalty is otherwise provided for it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is a subsequent offence under the same section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has been convicted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fine in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the imprisonment in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9C the sentence is within the penalty` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the person is guilty of a breach or an offence under this Act` AND (NOT `a penalty is otherwise provided for it`) AND `the person has been convicted`)
    THEN
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the penalty is for "any breach or any offence under this Act for which no penalty is otherwise provided", on conviction
        NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the fine and the term are within the ceilings` (`s 9C the penalty on conviction` `the offence is a subsequent offence under the same section`) `the fine in dollars` `the imprisonment in months`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or to both, and for a subsequent offence under the same section to a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or to both"
            JUST FALSE

§§ `Section 10 -- Composition of offences`

-- Which offences are compoundable is prescribed by regulations (section 10(3)) that are not among the sources, so
-- whether an offence is compoundable is a fact the case supplies.
-- src:1093 | 10.—(1) An investigating officer, with the approval of the
-- src:1094 | Commissioner, may compound any offence under this Act that is
-- src:1095 | prescribed as a compoundable offence by collecting from a person
-- src:1096 | reasonably suspected of having committed the offence a sum not
-- src:1097 | exceeding the lower of the following:
@ref s 10(1) (src:1093-1097)
GIVEN `the person acting is an investigating officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner has approved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is prescribed as a compoundable offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is reasonably suspected of having committed the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(1) the investigating officer may compound the offence` MEANS
    IF `the person acting is an investigating officer` AND `the Commissioner has approved` AND `the offence is prescribed as a compoundable offence` AND `the person is reasonably suspected of having committed the offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is of "An investigating officer, with the approval of the Commissioner" to compound "any offence under this Act that is prescribed as a compoundable offence" by collecting a sum from "a person reasonably suspected of having committed the offence"
        NOTHING

-- "a sum not exceeding the lower of (a) one half of the amount of the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence; (b) $1,000".
-- Every offence in this Act has a maximum fine of $5,000 or more (sections 4(3), 9(2), 9B(1), 9C, 8(7), 8B(13)), so one
-- half is $2,500 or more and the lower is $1,000 for each of them.
-- src:1093 | 10.—(1) An investigating officer, with the approval of the
-- src:1094 | Commissioner, may compound any offence under this Act that is
-- src:1095 | prescribed as a compoundable offence by collecting from a person
-- src:1096 | reasonably suspected of having committed the offence a sum not
-- src:1097 | exceeding the lower of the following:
-- src:1099 | (a) one half of the amount of the maximum fine that is
-- src:1100 | prescribed for the offence;
-- src:1102 | (b) $1,000.
@ref s 10(1) (src:1093-1102)
GIVEN `the maximum fine prescribed for the offence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 10(1) the largest sum that may be collected` MEANS
    min (`the maximum fine prescribed for the offence` DIVIDED BY 2) 1_000

-- src:1104 | (2) On payment of the sum of money, no further proceedings are to
-- src:1105 | be taken against that person in respect of the offence.
@ref s 10(2) (src:1104-1105)
GIVEN `the sum of money has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(2) further proceedings may be taken against the person in respect of the offence` MEANS
    IF `the sum of money has been paid`
    THEN
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On payment of the sum of money, no further proceedings are to be taken against that person in respect of the offence"
        JUST FALSE
    ELSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is "On payment of the sum of money"; it has not been paid
        NOTHING

§§ `Section 11 -- Exemption`

-- src:1112 | 11.—(1) The Minister may, by notification in the Gazette, exempt
-- src:1113 | with or without conditions any person or class of persons from all or
-- src:1114 | any of the provisions of this Act.
@ref s 11(1) (src:1112-1114)
GIVEN `the person or a class that includes the person is exempted by the Minister by notification in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision is within the exemption` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conditions of the exemption, if any, are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 11(1) the person is exempt from the provision` MEANS
    IF `the person or a class that includes the person is exempted by the Minister by notification in the Gazette` AND `the provision is within the exemption` AND `the conditions of the exemption, if any, are met`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exemption is of "any person or class of persons from all or any of the provisions of this Act", "by notification in the Gazette", "with or without conditions"
        NOTHING

-- src:1116 | (2) The Minister may at any time revoke any such exemption, vary
-- src:1117 | or revoke any existing conditions or impose new conditions.
@ref s 11(2) (src:1116-1117)
GIVEN `an exemption was granted under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 11(2) the Minister may revoke the exemption, vary or revoke its conditions, or impose new conditions` MEANS
    IF `an exemption was granted under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is over "any such exemption"
        NOTHING

§§ `Section 11A -- Restriction on contracting out`

-- "void insofar as it purports": the term is void to the extent that it does either thing.
-- src:1121 | 11A. Any term of a contract of service or collective agreement is
-- src:1122 | void insofar as it purports —
-- src:1124 | (a) to exclude or limit the operation of any provision of this
-- src:1125 | Act; or
-- src:1127 | (b) to preclude any person from making a representation, a
-- src:1128 | claim or an application under this Act.
@ref s 11A (src:1121-1128)
GIVEN `the term is a term of a contract of service or collective agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it purports to exclude or limit the operation of any provision of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it purports to preclude any person from making a representation, a claim or an application under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 11A the term is void insofar as it so purports` MEANS
    IF `the term is a term of a contract of service or collective agreement` AND (`it purports to exclude or limit the operation of any provision of this Act` OR `it purports to preclude any person from making a representation, a claim or an application under this Act`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the term is void "insofar as it purports" (a) to exclude or limit the operation of any provision of this Act or (b) to preclude any person from making a representation, a claim or an application under this Act
        NOTHING

§§ `Section 11B -- Power to issue tripartite guidelines`

-- "regard may be had": a permission, not a duty (compare section 7C(5), which says the employer must take them into account)
-- (fork F15).
-- src:1137 | 11B. The Minister may issue guidelines relating to the
-- src:1138 | re-employment of eligible employees and the terms and conditions
-- src:1139 | of re-employment of eligible employees, in the form of tripartite
-- src:1140 | guidelines, and upon the publication of such guidelines in the
-- src:1141 | Gazette, regard may be had to the guidelines for the purposes of Part 3
-- src:1142 | and sections 8A, 8B and 8C of this Act and section 34 of the Industrial
-- src:1143 | Relations Act 1960.
@ref s 11B (src:1137-1143)
GIVEN `the guidelines relate to the re-employment of eligible employees and the terms and conditions of their re-employment, in the form of tripartite guidelines` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the guidelines have been published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is Part 3, section 8A, 8B or 8C of this Act or section 34 of the Industrial Relations Act 1960` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 11B regard may be had to the guidelines for the purpose` MEANS
    IF `the guidelines relate to the re-employment of eligible employees and the terms and conditions of their re-employment, in the form of tripartite guidelines` AND `the guidelines have been published in the Gazette` AND `the purpose is Part 3, section 8A, 8B or 8C of this Act or section 34 of the Industrial Relations Act 1960`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "upon the publication of such guidelines in the Gazette, regard may be had to the guidelines for the purposes of Part 3 and sections 8A, 8B and 8C of this Act and section 34 of the Industrial Relations Act 1960"; the case falls outside
        NOTHING

§§ `Section 13 -- Saving of other written law`

-- src:1186 | 13. Nothing in this Act operates to relieve any employer of any duty
-- src:1187 | or liability imposed upon the employer by the provisions of any other
-- src:1188 | written law for the time being in force.
@ref s 13 (src:1186-1188)
GIVEN `the duty or liability is imposed on the employer by the provisions of another written law for the time being in force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 13 this Act relieves the employer of the duty or liability` MEANS
    IF `the duty or liability is imposed on the employer by the provisions of another written law for the time being in force`
    THEN
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this Act operates to relieve any employer of any duty or liability imposed upon the employer by the provisions of any other written law for the time being in force"
        JUST FALSE
    ELSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the saving is of "any duty or liability imposed upon the employer by the provisions of any other written law"
        NOTHING
